    <body>
      <sec><title>Introduction</title>
        <p>Septic shock is sepsis with persistent hypotension that needs vasopressors to keep the mean arterial pressure at or above 65 mmHg, together with a raised serum lactate despite adequate fluids.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec><title>Treatment / Management</title>
        <p>Norepinephrine is the first-line vasopressor. Vasopressin may be added when the norepinephrine dose rises. Patients who need high vasopressor doses on the first day stay longer in intensive care.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec><title>Enhancing Healthcare Team Outcomes</title><p>An interprofessional team approach is crucial; this boilerplate section must be skipped.</p></sec>
      <sec><title>Disclosure</title><p>Disclosure text that must be skipped.</p></sec>
    </body>
